0..79 Comment "// A record type\'s faces: each a set of the record\'s labels, named in a `where`"
80..158 Comment "// block after the type. A static bracket after the type fixes some fields, by"
159..179 Comment "// label or by face."
180..182 Comment "//"
183..259 Comment "// A record type\'s labels are its boundary. A face over them names a part of"
260..334 Comment "// the record, so a later form restricts a value to that part. The checker"
335..413 Comment "// checks each fixed value at its field\'s type. A value of the patched type is"
414..492 Comment "// the record of its free fields, and a literal can state a fixed field at its"
493..573 Comment "// fixed value. A name at it reads a fixed field as the value the bracket fixes."
574..576 Comment "//"
577..654 Comment "// The block names each face as a theory\'s `face` member does. The block ends"
655..734 Comment "// the type member at its `}`, as a `data` block ends its declaration. A record"
735..803 Comment "// type with no block keeps its labels as its boundary all the same."
804..872 Comment "// `Config[.port = 443, .tls = true]` fixes two fields by label, and"
873..949 Comment "// `Config[secure ↦ *{.port = 443, .tls = true}]` fixes the face `secure`."
950..981 Comment "// `|->` spells `↦` in ASCII."
982..984 Comment "//"
985..1063 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/record-faces.gandr` — a face past the labels, a"
1064..1143 Comment "//   face named twice, a bracket naming a field or a face the type lacks, and a"
1144..1204 Comment "//   literal stating a fixed field at another value, refused"
1205..1284 Comment "// - see: `model/desc/shaped-signature.gandr` — a theory\'s `boundary` and its"
1285..1295 Comment "//   faces"
1296..1358 Comment "// - owes: #5578 — a configuration coerced to a patched type"
1359..1428 Comment "// - owes: #5579 — an element of a patched type coerced back to the"
1429..1447 Comment "//   configuration"
1448..1528 Comment "// - owes: #5106 — two faces fixed at once, whose values agree where the faces"
1529..1538 Comment "//   meet"
